Pairs: $(1, 3)$ since $1 \le 3/2$ (1.5) -> $1 \le 1.5$ True. $(2, 4)$ since $2 \le 4/2$ (2) -> $2 \le 2$ True.
Wait, $1 \le 3/2$ is true. $2 \le 4/2$ is true.
Can we do better? No, 4 elements, max 2 pairs.
Sample 1, Query 2: $A[3 \dots 8] = \{2, 3, 4, 4, 7, 10\}$.
Pairs: $(2, 4)$, $(3, 7)$, $(4, 10)$.
$2 \le 4/2$ (2) -> OK.
$3 \le 7/2$ (3.5) -> OK.
$4 \le 10/2$ (5) -> OK.
Total 3.
