However, the condition is $A_i \le \frac{A_j}{2}$.
Since $A_i \ge 1$ and $A_j \ge 1$, if $A_i \le A_j/2$, then $A_i < A_j$.
Since the array is sorted, if $A_i \le A_j/2$, then $i < j$ must hold (unless $A_i = A_j = 0$, but sizes are $\ge 1$).
So we are looking for the number of pairs $(i, j)$ with $1 \le i < j \le N$ such that $A_i \le \frac{A_j}{2}$.
