The problem asks us to calculate the sum of $f(P)$ over all permutations $P$ of the sequence $(1, 2, \ldots, N)$, modulo 998244353.
Here, $f(P)$ is formed by concatenating the decimal representations of the numbers in the permutation $P$.
Let $P = (A_1, A_2, \ldots, A_N)$. Then $f(P)$ is the integer formed by concatenating $A_1, A_2, \ldots, A_N$.
Mathematically, if $L(A_i)$ denotes the number of digits in $A_i$, then
$f(P) = \sum_{i=1}^N A_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N L(A_j)}$.
We need to compute $\sum_{P} f(P) \pmod{998244353}$.

Let's rewrite the sum:
Total Sum $= \sum_{P} \sum_{i=1}^N A_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N L(A_j)}$.
We can swap the summations:
Total Sum $= \sum_{i=1}^N \sum_{P} A_i \cdot 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N L(A_j)}$.

The term $A_i$ depends on the value at the $i$-th position in the permutation.
The term $10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N L(A_j)}$ depends on the lengths of the numbers at positions $i+1, \ldots, N$.
Let $S_i = \sum_{j=i+1}^N L(A_j)$. This is the total number of digits contributed by elements placed after position $i$.
So we need to calculate $\sum_{P} A_i \cdot 10^{S_i}$.

Let's fix the position $i$ in the permutation. We want to sum $A_i \cdot 10^{S_i}$ over all permutations.
The value $A_i$ can be any number from $1$ to $N$.
The exponent $S_i$ depends on the set of numbers placed in positions $i+1, \ldots, N$.
Let $U = \{1, 2, \ldots, N\}$.
Suppose we choose a subset $K \subset U$ of size $N-i$ to be placed in positions $i+1, \ldots, N$.
Let $L(K) = \sum_{x \in K} L(x)$.
Then for a fixed subset $K$ and a fixed value $v \in U \setminus K$ (which will be at position $i$), the contribution is $v \cdot 10^{L(K)}$.
The number of ways to arrange the elements of $K$ in positions $i+1, \ldots, N$ is $(N-i)!$.
The number of ways to arrange the remaining elements in positions $1, \ldots, i-1$ is $(i-1)!$.
So, for a fixed position $i$, the total contribution is:
$\sum_{K \subset U, |K|=N-i} \sum_{v \in U \setminus K} v \cdot 10^{L(K)} \cdot (N-i)! \cdot (i-1)!$.
We can factor out the factorials:
$(N-i)! (i-1)! \sum_{K \subset U, |K|=N-i} 10^{L(K)} \left( \sum_{v \in U \setminus K} v \right)$.

Let $S_{total} = \sum_{x=1}^N x = \frac{N(N+1)}{2}$.
Then $\sum_{v \in U \setminus K} v = S_{total} - \sum_{x \in K} x$.
So the term becomes:
$(N-i)! (i-1)! \sum_{K \subset U, |K|=N-i} 10^{L(K)} (S_{total} - \sum_{x \in K} x)$.
Let $m = N-i$. We are summing over subsets of size $m$.
The term is $\sum_{K, |K|=m} 10^{L(K)} (S_{total} - \sum_{x \in K} x)$.
